      "panel-1": {
        "kind": "Panel",
        "spec": {
          "id": 1,
          "title": "15.1 / 15.2 instructions",
          "description": "",
          "links": [],
          "data": {
            "kind": "QueryGroup",
            "spec": {
              "queries": [],
              "transformations": [],
              "queryOptions": {}
            }
          },
          "vizConfig": {
            "kind": "VizConfig",
            "group": "text",
            "version": "",
            "spec": {
              "options": {
                "mode": "markdown",
                "content": "## 15.1 / 15.2 - Inspect Data tab and CSV download\n\n**15.1 Inspect > Data (visual)**\n1. On **Multi-frame table** (two queries with different columns), open the panel menu > **Inspect > Data**.\n2. Use the frame picker to switch between frame A (random walk table) and frame B (CSV hosts). Also try \"Series joined by time\".\n3. Toggle **Formatted data** and **Apply panel transformations** on and off. The table panel has an Organize fields transform: with transforms on, frame B shows **Hostname** and **Latency (ms)** instead of Host and Latency ms. The time series panel has a Join by field transform: with transforms on, both series become one frame, so the frame picker shows a single frame.\n4. Repeat on **Time series, two queries**.\n5. Compare the inspect table with a normal table panel, for example the [Kitchen Sink](/d/dcb9f5e9-8066-4397-889e-864b99555dbb).\n\n**Expected:** the inspect table uses the new TableNG look (same header, cell padding, fonts, borders, scroll bars as other TableNG tables). Switching frames and toggles updates the rows and columns with no layout jump, blank table, or console error.\n\n**15.2 CSV download for Excel**\n1. In Inspect > Data, open **Data options** and turn on **Download for Excel**.\n2. Click **Download CSV** for each frame (and for \"Series joined by time\" on the time series panel).\n3. Open each file in Excel.\n\n**Expected:** Excel opens the file without an import wizard; headers match the column names shown in Inspect; each frame's rows and values match what Inspect shows (no shifted columns, no mangled characters, numbers stay numbers).\n"
              },
              "fieldConfig": {
                "defaults": {},
                "overrides": []
              }
            }
          }
        }
      },
