            "spec": {
              "options": {
                "mode": "markdown",
                "content": "## 15.3 - Raw Prometheus table in Explore\n\nNeeds Prometheus from devenv: `make devenv sources=prometheus` (datasource `gdev-prometheus`, http://localhost:9090). Explore state cannot be provisioned, so the link carries it.\n\n1. [Open prometheus_http_requests_total (instant) in Explore](/explore?schemaVersion=1&panes=%7B%22a1b%22%3A%7B%22datasource%22%3A%22gdev-prometheus%22%2C%22queries%22%3A%5B%7B%22refId%22%3A%22A%22%2C%22datasource%22%3A%7B%22type%22%3A%22prometheus%22%2C%22uid%22%3A%22gdev-prometheus%22%7D%2C%22expr%22%3A%22prometheus_http_requests_total%22%2C%22instant%22%3Atrue%2C%22range%22%3Afalse%2C%22editorMode%22%3A%22code%22%7D%5D%2C%22range%22%3A%7B%22from%22%3A%22now-1h%22%2C%22to%22%3A%22now%22%7D%7D%7D&orgId=1).\n2. Run the query if it did not run. In the results, switch the table to **Raw** view.\n3. Sort by a few columns (a label column and the Value column).\n4. Use the column header filter on a label column (for example `handler` or `code`).\n5. Make the window narrower and wider.\n\n**Expected:** Raw view renders every series as a row in the new table, with all labels and the value. Sort and filter work. Long label sets give sensible column widths (no columns squashed to nothing, no very wide empty columns), and the table scrolls instead of overflowing. No console errors.\n"
              },
              "fieldConfig": {
                "defaults": {},
                "overrides": []
              }
            }
          }
        }
